-- title:
--   Construct every requested level of a shared reporting catalog
-- statement:
--   Let $f,g$ be integer subset functions on $[512hJ]$, bounded by $B,C$ on sets of size at most $2hJ$. Their complete suffix-zeta tables and pointer cells lie before record base $r_0$. Reserve $5K$ record cells ending before payload base $a$, where $K\le\lfloor13J/20\rfloor+1$.
--
--   Assume $S\le W$ and the stated multi-level resource contract: the complete payload fits space; control values, powers, prefix keys, sorted indices, suffix values, and switches fit words; and every pair, width, and sort call fits the depth limit. The routine returns $a_K$, the prescribed payload endpoint, and establishes
--   $$\forall k<K,\quad\text{record }r_0+5k\text{ describes the exact catalog at }a_k.$$
--   Each level uses the computed switch threshold and residual box cutoff. Time is the sum of the defined round budgets, including eight loop steps per level, plus $100$. Memory before $r_0$, and memory below $a$ outside the records, is preserved.
--
--   This builds all reusable reporting levels for one pair of source functions.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/c0ldzy17/three-sum-lean/blob/2b639655e07421b9ac743de9090459bab473a7c0/Submission/ThreeSum/LightSharedReportingLevels.lean#L68-L198

